Description: os-support: build SlowBcopy.c on the BSDs.
 xf86SlowBcopy() is exported in the SDK (xf86_OSproc.h) and used by
 compiler.h's slowbcopy_tobus()/slowbcopy_frombus(), but 25.1.9 builds
 misc/SlowBcopy.c only for Linux and the stub OS, so a driver that uses it
 fails to load on FreeBSD with an undefined symbol.
 Unchanged from FreeBSD's port (which builds 25.1.9); it applies to 25.1.9
 as it is.
Origin: FreeBSD ports, x11-servers/xlibre-server/files/patch-hw_xfree86_os-support_meson.build
 (https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports/blob/956f979f4876d6ea542f5fdae60d8b7166b87345/x11-servers/xlibre-server/files/patch-hw_xfree86_os-support_meson.build)
Forwarded: not yet; a candidate for X11Libre (missing exported symbol on BSD)
---
diff --git a/hw/xfree86/os-support/meson.build b/hw/xfree86/os-support/meson.build
index 18bcc8d..1017b91 100644
--- a/hw/xfree86/os-support/meson.build
+++ b/hw/xfree86/os-support/meson.build
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ elif host_machine.system().endswith('bsd') or host_machine.system() == 'dragonfl
         'bsd/bsd_bell.c',
         'bsd/bsd_init.c',
         'shared/drm_platform.c',
+        'misc/SlowBcopy.c',
 	'shared/pm_noop.c'
     ]
 
